# PipRail × Hermes — copy to ~/.hermes/.env and fill in. NEVER commit a real key.
# Hermes reads ${VAR} references from ~/.hermes/.env at connect time; the config.yaml
# mcp_servers.piprail.env block references PIPRAIL_PRIVATE_KEY as ${PIPRAIL_PRIVATE_KEY}.
# (chmod 600 ~/.hermes/.env)

# REQUIRED to pay — a funded wallet key/seed for the chain below. OMIT for read-only mode
# (discover/quote/register/budget/guide work key-less; pay/plan return WALLET_REQUIRED).
# EVM: 0x… hex private key. Solana: base58 secret. Or a 12/24-word mnemonic.
PIPRAIL_PRIVATE_KEY=0xYOUR_PRIVATE_KEY

# Chain to pay on. EVM ('base' default, 'ethereum', 'polygon', 'arbitrum', 'bnb', …)
# or 'solana' | 'ton' | 'tron' | 'near' | 'sui' | 'aptos' | 'algorand' | 'stellar' | 'xrpl'.
PIPRAIL_CHAIN=base

# Spend policy — the agent CANNOT exceed these (human units).
PIPRAIL_MAX_AMOUNT=0.10      # max per payment
PIPRAIL_MAX_TOTAL=5.00       # lifetime cap, per token
PIPRAIL_TOKENS=USDC          # allowed tokens (comma-separated)

# Optional: add the standard x402 'exact' rail so the agent can pay any standard x402 server.
# PIPRAIL_SCHEMES=onchain-proof,exact

# Optional: your own RPC endpoint (recommended in production; fold any API key into the URL).
# PIPRAIL_RPC_URL=https://...
